{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are GateSter's Stage 0 Question Analyzer. Analyze raw GATE CS/IT questions and return ONLY a structured Stage 0 Blueprint JSON."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Analyze this GATE question:\n\nCache size is determined by the 12 bits for indexing, which means there are 212 = 4096 blocks. The size of each block is 1 byte. So, the cache size is 4096 bytes, or 4 Kb. Alternate Solution: Tag bits = 4 bits Cache has 16 blocks Block size = 1 Byte = 8 bits Mapping type = Direct Mapped Cache Address is divided into three parts: TAG | Line (Index) | Word Offset TAG = 4 bits Remaining bits (Line + Offset) = 12 bits Total address size = 16 bits Cache Size (CM): Number of blocks = 16 = 24 Block size = 1 Byte"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Computer Organization and Architecture\",\n  \"topic\": \"Machine Instructions & Addressing Modes\",\n  \"core_concept\": \"Understanding cache organization and addressing modes\",\n  \"question_type\": \"MCQ\",\n  \"requires_calculation\": false,\n  \"mutable_fields\": [],\n  \"immutable_fields\": [],\n  \"transformation_rules\": [],\n  \"question_id\": \"GATE_0_Q621\",\n  \"year\": 0,\n  \"question\": \"Cache size is determined by the 12 bits for indexing, which means there are 212 = 4096 blocks. The size of each block is 1 byte. So, the cache size is 4096 bytes, or 4 Kb. Alternate Solution: Tag bits = 4 bits Cache has 16 blocks Block size = 1 Byte = 8 bits Mapping type = Direct Mapped Cache Address is divided into three parts: TAG | Line (Index) | Word Offset TAG = 4 bits Remaining bits (Line + Offset) = 12 bits Total address size = 16 bits Cache Size (CM): Number of blocks = 16 = 24 Block size = 1 Byte\",\n  \"options\": [],\n  \"retrieved_go_classes_notes\": [\n    \"Fixed size at compile time (for static arrays).\\nZero-indexed: The first element is at index 0.\\nArray name decays to a pointer to its first element in most contexts.\\nAddress Calculation (1D Array):\\nAddress Calculation (2D Array, Row-Major):\\nwhere cols is the number of columns in the array.\\nCommon Pitfalls or Tricky Points:\\nArray out-of-bounds access: Accessing elements beyond the declared size leads to undefined behavior.\",\n    \"Answer key\\u261f\\nBasic Blocks (2)\\nBasic Blocks: GATE CSE 2025 | Set 1 | Question: 42\\nRefer to the given -address code sequence. This code sequence is split into basic blocks. The number of\\nbasic blocks is ________. (Answer in integer)\\n1001: i = 1\\n1002: j = 1\\n1003: t1 = 10*i\\n1004: t2 = t1+j\\n1005: t3 = 8*t2\\n1006: t4 = t3-88\\n1007: a[t4] = 0.0\\n1008: j = j+1\\n1009: if j <= 10 goto 1003\\n1010: i = i+1\\n1011: if i <= 10 goto 1002\\n1012: i = 1\\n1013: t5 = i-1\\n1014: t6 = 88*t5\\n1015: a[t6] = 1.0\\n1016: i = i+1\"\n  ]\n}"}]}
