{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are GateSter's Stage 0 Question Analyzer. Analyze raw GATE CS/IT questions and return ONLY a structured Stage 0 Blueprint JSON."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Analyze this GATE question:\n\n+ 1 is written as 1011, which consists of 4 bits so, append 3 bits of Os to the message.\n\nM = 11000000\n\n538\n\nCOMPUTER NETWORK\n\nCheck Out Our GATE Courses & Secure Your Dream Rank!\n\nThere the check bits sequence is 100.\n\n8. ANSWER:- A\n\nc1 = d11 \u2295 d9 \u2295 d7 \u2295 d5 \u2295 d3\n\nFor even parity, the total modulo-2 sum of the check bit and its associated data bits must equal 0 :\n         c1 \u2295 d11 \u2295 d9 \u2295 d7 \u2295 d5 \u2295 d3 = 0 (mod2)\n\nSubstitute the known values from the tables:\n0 \u2295 1 \u2295 x \u2295 0 \u2295 0 \u2295 1 = 0 (mod2)\n         Simplify the numbers (remembering that 1 \u2295 1 = 0 ):\n0 \u2295 x = 0 (mod2)\n\nx = 0\n\n9. ANSWER:- 51\n\nThe time taken for a packet (Tt(packet)):\n\nTt(packet) = L / B.W = 2000 bits / 106 bps = 2 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 sec = 2 msec\n\nThe time taken for an acknowledgement (Tt(Ack)):\n\nTt(Ack) = 10 bits / 106 bps = 10\u207b\u2075 sec = 10\u207b\u00b2 msec = 0.01 msec\n\nTp = 100 msec\n\nThe total time (Total time):\n\nTotal time = Tt(packet) + 2 * Tp + Tt(Ack) = 2 msec + 200 msec + 0.01 msec = 202.01 msec\n\nEfficiency Calculation:\n\nEfficiency (e) = useful time / total time\n\n  e = n * Tt(packet) / (Total time)\n\n  n >= 0.5 * 202.01 / 2 >= 101.005 / 2 >= 50.5025\n\nhence the window size is 51."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Compiler Design\",\n  \"topic\": \"Three Address Code\",\n  \"core_concept\": \"Identification and counting of basic blocks in a three address code sequence\",\n  \"question_type\": \"NAT\",\n  \"requires_calculation\": false,\n  \"mutable_fields\": [],\n  \"immutable_fields\": [],\n  \"transformation_rules\": [],\n  \"question_id\": \"GATE_0_Q671\",\n  \"year\": 0,\n  \"question\": \"+ 1 is written as 1011, which consists of 4 bits so, append 3 bits of Os to the message.\\n\\nM = 11000000\\n\\n538\\n\\nCOMPUTER NETWORK\\n\\nCheck Out Our GATE Courses & Secure Your Dream Rank!\\n\\nThere the check bits sequence is 100.\\n\\n8. ANSWER:- A\\n\\nc1 = d11 \\u2295 d9 \\u2295 d7 \\u2295 d5 \\u2295 d3\\n\\nFor even parity, the total modulo-2 sum of the check bit and its associated data bits must equal 0 :\\n         c1 \\u2295 d11 \\u2295 d9 \\u2295 d7 \\u2295 d5 \\u2295 d3 = 0 (mod2)\\n\\nSubstitute the known values from the tables:\\n0 \\u2295 1 \\u2295 x \\u2295 0 \\u2295 0 \\u2295 1 = 0 (mod2)\\n         Simplify the numbers (remembering that 1 \\u2295 1 = 0 ):\\n0 \\u2295 x = 0 (mod2)\\n\\nx = 0\\n\\n9. ANSWER:- 51\\n\\nThe time taken for a packet (Tt(packet)):\\n\\nTt(packet) = L / B.W = 2000 bits / 106 bps = 2 \\u00d7 10\\u207b\\u00b3 sec = 2 msec\\n\\nThe time taken for an acknowledgement (Tt(Ack)):\\n\\nTt(Ack) = 10 bits / 106 bps = 10\\u207b\\u2075 sec = 10\\u207b\\u00b2 msec = 0.01 msec\\n\\nTp = 100 msec\\n\\nThe total time (Total time):\\n\\nTotal time = Tt(packet) + 2 * Tp + Tt(Ack) = 2 msec + 200 msec + 0.01 msec = 202.01 msec\\n\\nEfficiency Calculation:\\n\\nEfficiency (e) = useful time / total time\\n\\n  e = n * Tt(packet) / (Total time)\\n\\n  n >= 0.5 * 202.01 / 2 >= 101.005 / 2 >= 50.5025\\n\\nhence the window size is 51.\",\n  \"options\": [],\n  \"retrieved_go_classes_notes\": [\n    \"1014: t6 = 88*t5\\n1015: a[t6] = 1.0\\n1016: i = i+1\\n1017: if i <= 10 goto 1013\\n \\ngatecse2025-set1 compiler-design three-address-code basic-blocks numerical-answers easy two-marks\\nAnswer key\\u261f\",\n    \"Answer key\\u261f\\nBasic Blocks (2)\\nBasic Blocks: GATE CSE 2025 | Set 1 | Question: 42\\nRefer to the given -address code sequence. This code sequence is split into basic blocks. The number of\\nbasic blocks is ________. (Answer in integer)\\n1001: i = 1\\n1002: j = 1\\n1003: t1 = 10*i\\n1004: t2 = t1+j\\n1005: t3 = 8*t2\\n1006: t4 = t3-88\\n1007: a[t4] = 0.0\\n1008: j = j+1\\n1009: if j <= 10 goto 1003\\n1010: i = i+1\\n1011: if i <= 10 goto 1002\\n1012: i = 1\\n1013: t5 = i-1\\n1014: t6 = 88*t5\\n1015: a[t6] = 1.0\\n1016: i = i+1\"\n  ]\n}"}]}
